.TH GGE\-DRAWING 7 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
gge\-drawing \- primitives, sprites, text, tilemaps, cameras
.SH DESCRIPTION
All drawing happens inside a scene's
.B render
callback, in logical pixels (EngineConfig.logical_w x logical_h; the window is
scaled to fit). Later calls paint over earlier ones. Colors are
.B Color
{r,g,b,a} 0..255 built with
.BR rgb (),
.BR rgba ()
or the
.B COLOR_*
constants; rectangles are
.B Rect
{x,y,w,h} built with
.BR rect ().
.SS Primitives (draw.h)
.BR draw_clear ", " draw_rect ", " draw_rect_outline ", " draw_line ", " draw_point ", "
.BR draw_texture ", " draw_texture_ex ", " draw_debug_text .
Alpha blending is always on, so
.B rgba(0,0,0,160)
over the whole screen dims whatever was drawn beneath.
.SS Sprites (sprite.h)
.BR sprite_from (3)
slices a texture into equal frames.
.BR sprite_draw (3),
.BR sprite_draw_scaled (3),
.BR sprite_draw_tinted (3)
draw one frame; frame index = column + row * columns.
.B Anim
/
.B AnimState
with
.BR anim_step (3)
and
.BR anim_frame (3)
play ranges of frames. Tinting multiplies a white sheet by a color, which is
how palette\-free recolouring works: draw layered white silhouettes with
different tints.
.SS Text (text.h)
.BR text_load_font (3)
(needs ENGINE_WITH_TTF and EngineConfig.text; falls back to the 8px debug
font when the file is missing),
.BR text_draw (3),
.BR text_size (3)
for measuring and centering.
.SS Tilemaps and cameras
A
.B Tilemap
is a uint8_t grid plus a tileset sprite; frame 0 is empty. Fill it from code
or
.BR tilemap_load_csv (3)
(Tiled export). A
.B Camera
converts world to screen;
.BR camera_follow (3)
tracks a target,
.BR tilemap_draw (3)
draws only the visible tiles.
.SS Smooth motion
Draw at
.BR v2_lerp "(prev, now, alpha)" ;
keep prev in a scene static updated at the start of each
.BR update .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR draw_rect (3),
.BR sprite_draw (3),
.BR text_draw (3),
.BR tilemap_draw (3),
.BR camera_follow (3),
.BR gge\-assets (7)
